title: 'statement-store: bound inbound statement batch size'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    An inbound statement notification is now rejected from its length prefix, before decoding, when
    it declares more statements than a notification can hold, so a peer can't turn a small message
    into a large allocation before the rate limiter runs. Such a peer is disconnected; other decode
    failures stay a bad-message report.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: minor
